<title>INDIA: India approves Bharti Tele Ventures' $122 mln plan.</title>
<headline>India approves Bharti Tele Ventures' $122 mln plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Industry Ministry on Monday approved a proposal by Bharti Tele Ventures Ltd to set up an investing company with 4.38 billion rupees ($122 million) in foreign investment, an official statement said.</p>
<p>The ministry also approved a proposal by Asea Brown Boveri Ltd to set up a wholly owned investment company with foreign investment of two billion rupees, it said.</p>
<p>The ministry approved 53 foreign direct investment proposals in all, worth a total of 17.95 billion rupees, it said. ($1 = 35.8 rupees)</p>
</text>
